title: MSBuild Pre-Build Event or Public Pictures Staging Launching Script Hosts
id: 645f3b78-4c71-4ff2-9efa-242c36cd268a
status: experimental
description: Detects the build-time execution pattern used by fake "security tool" GitHub repositories that hide PowerShell in Visual Studio PreBuildEvent routines and stage an Electron-based loader named Microsoft.exe under C:\Users\Public\Pictures. Flags MSBuild spawning a script host, and any process launched from that staging directory.
references:
  - https://news.drweb.com/show/?c=5&i=15311&lng=en
  - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/fake-security-tools-on-github-push-backdoors-and-infostealers/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/08
tags:
  - attack.t1195
  - attack.t1059
  - attack.t1105
  - attack.initial-access
  - attack.execution
logsource:
  category: process_creation
  product: windows
detection:
  selection_build_parent:
    ParentImage|endswith: '\MSBuild.exe'
  selection_script_host:
    Image|endswith:
      - '\powershell.exe'
      - '\pwsh.exe'
      - '\cmd.exe'
      - '\mshta.exe'
  selection_public_pictures_cmd:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '\Users\Public\Pictures\'
      - '/Users/Public/Pictures/'
  selection_public_pictures_img:
    Image|contains:
      - '\Users\Public\Pictures\'
      - '/Users/Public/Pictures/'
  filter_build_script_known:
    CommandLine|contains:
      - '\Microsoft Visual Studio\'
      - '\MSBuild\Current\Bin\'
      - 'dotnet msbuild'
  condition: (selection_build_parent and selection_script_host and not filter_build_script_known) or selection_public_pictures_cmd or selection_public_pictures_img
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate Visual Studio projects with PreBuildEvent steps that run PowerShell for code generation or versioning
  - Enterprise build pipelines that stage signed binaries under Public\Pictures (rare; validate the parent process and signer)
level: high
